(338492, 26027, 7908, '<td valign="top">Here is my 10 for this challenge! I love how they seem to be refusing to "follow her". If I was going to nitpick, I would like the little guy on the left either completely in or out ... of course, then you run into the next one. What to do?</td>', 'Here is my 10 for this challenge! I love how they seem to be refusing to "follow her". If I was going to nitpick, I would like the little guy on the left either completely in or out ... of course, then you run into the next one. What to do?', '2003-06-25 23:05:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(338497, 26098, 772, '<td valign="top">I think this is a beautiful photo of a country/rural environment.  I wish you had put half as much thought into the titles as you did the photo :)  I believe that a title is an integral part of the photo when they are both presented together.  Your title makes me feel like you don''t really care much for the image.  This photo, for me, is a ''window into the past'' or ''retrospective view'' or ''time portal'' or something that supports/enhances the essence of what you have captured in this image.  This photo is obviously well thought out and well executed.  After planning and pursuing a nice image like this, why not take the extra effort to ''put the cherry on top'' with a nice title?  = 9</td>', 'I think this is a beautiful photo of a country/rural environment.  I wish you had put half as much thought into the titles as you did the photo :)  I believe that a title is an integral part of the photo when they are both presented together.  Your title makes me feel like you don''t really care much for the image.  This photo, for me, is a ''window into the past'' or ''retrospective view'' or ''time portal'' or something that supports/enhances the essence of what you have captured in this image.  This photo is obviously well thought out and well executed.  After planning and pursuing a nice image like this, why not take the extra effort to ''put the cherry on top'' with a nice title?  = 9', '2003-06-25 23:10:53.000000', NULL, 1),
