(339965, 26079, 6349, '<td valign="top">This is my favorite shot for the challenge.  I really hope this wins.  The lines undulating line of the road going into the distance blends beautifully with the horizontal soft whisps of clouds and the location and apparel of the subject is just right.  Great job!  Looking forward to congratulating whoever this is again when the challenge is over...</td>', 'This is my favorite shot for the challenge.  I really hope this wins.  The lines undulating line of the road going into the distance blends beautifully with the horizontal soft whisps of clouds and the location and apparel of the subject is just right.  Great job!  Looking forward to congratulating whoever this is again when the challenge is over...', '2003-06-27 07:41:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(339966, 26339, 6349, '<td valign="top">Strangely, I really love the background in this shot, the fence and barrel, but not the subject, since it is so tattered you can''t really make it out.  It''s also harder to distinguish because it blends in with the ground, whereas the rest is complimented well by the blue sky.  Hey!  You should have put it on top of the barrel!  It''s a fine photo non the less.  Good luck</td>', 'Strangely, I really love the background in this shot, the fence and barrel, but not the subject, since it is so tattered you can''t really make it out.  It''s also harder to distinguish because it blends in with the ground, whereas the rest is complimented well by the blue sky.  Hey!  You should have put it on top of the barrel!  It''s a fine photo non the less.  Good luck', '2003-06-27 07:44:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(339967, 26331, 6349, '<td valign="top">It''s good to actually see a person in one of these shots working.  That displays "country life" really well.  They''re living it.  Good job.</td>', 'It''s good to actually see a person in one of these shots working.  That displays "country life" really well.  They''re living it.  Good job.', '2003-06-27 07:44:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(339968, 25846, 6349, '<td valign="top">I really like this photo, but the details tend to blur together a bit, even though I''m sure they''re in focus.  Perhaps this has to do with the small resizing limits?  Anyway, nice capture.</td>', 'I really like this photo, but the details tend to blur together a bit, even though I''m sure they''re in focus.  Perhaps this has to do with the small resizing limits?  Anyway, nice capture.', '2003-06-27 07:46:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(339969, 26150, 3735, '<td valign="top">Watch that first step!!    Did you try useing auto levels, brighting and contrast. i thank would have cleared it up just a tad . but this is great.  9</td>', 'Watch that first step!!    Did you try useing auto levels, brighting and contrast. i thank would have cleared it up just a tad . but this is great.  9', '2003-06-27 07:46:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(339970, 25919, 8274, '<td valign="top">The trail leading away makes this picture</td>', 'The trail leading away makes this picture', '2003-06-27 07:47:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(339971, 25324, 6349, '<td valign="top">That''s pretty cute.  So much so that I think maybe a zoomed in shot would have been more effective.  As it is, the photo seems unbalanced with the heavy branches filling the frame on top and the tree being crooked.  Overall, a really nice scene that''s sure to lead to many wonderful photos.  Moving in on the subject would add more focus and detail to it and make the image simpler and more powerful.</td>', 'That''s pretty cute.  So much so that I think maybe a zoomed in shot would have been more effective.  As it is, the photo seems unbalanced with the heavy branches filling the frame on top and the tree being crooked.  Overall, a really nice scene that''s sure to lead to many wonderful photos.  Moving in on the subject would add more focus and detail to it and make the image simpler and more powerful.', '2003-06-27 07:48:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(339972, 25435, 6349, '<td valign="top">It''s a 10.  Oh yes, it is a 10.  Love it.  Nothing I can say to improve this at all.  At first I was going to suggest a tiny bit of darkening, but then I thought about it and realized that it would take away from the feeling of the dog resting in the hot glare of the sun and would also lose the detail inside the door which I like.  Superb photo.  I''m guessing it''s ribbon material.</td>', 'It''s a 10.  Oh yes, it is a 10.  Love it.  Nothing I can say to improve this at all.  At first I was going to suggest a tiny bit of darkening, but then I thought about it and realized that it would take away from the feeling of the dog resting in the hot glare of the sun and would also lose the detail inside the door which I like.  Superb photo.  I''m guessing it''s ribbon material.', '2003-06-27 07:50:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(339973, 25935, 6349, '<td valign="top">Very nice scene.  Looks like a peaceful picnic kinda place.  Something about the darkness on the left and how it spreads over the river is slightly bothersome, but that isn''t your fault of course.  Nice job.  Good luck.</td>', 'Very nice scene.  Looks like a peaceful picnic kinda place.  Something about the darkness on the left and how it spreads over the river is slightly bothersome, but that isn''t your fault of course.  Nice job.  Good luck.', '2003-06-27 07:51:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(339974, 25956, 6349, '<td valign="top">I like the soft tones in this and I''d really like to know how this effect was achieved.  Do you do wit with a lens on the camera or with some sort of photoshop post processing.  I can make images look like this in PS, but all the ways I can do it well are illegal, so I can never submit anything.  Let me know if you can.  Oh, and don''t worry, I''m not going to request a DQ or anything.  I''m not one of those people :)</td>', 'I like the soft tones in this and I''d really like to know how this effect was achieved.  Do you do wit with a lens on the camera or with some sort of photoshop post processing.  I can make images look like this in PS, but all the ways I can do it well are illegal, so I can never submit anything.  Let me know if you can.  Oh, and don''t worry, I''m not going to request a DQ or anything.  I''m not one of those people :)', '2003-06-27 07:53:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(339975, 25591, 6349, '<td valign="top">The colors seem oversaturated in this and the light in the sky is a bit harsh.  Otherwise, it is an interesting shot with a lot of potential.</td>', 'The colors seem oversaturated in this and the light in the sky is a bit harsh.  Otherwise, it is an interesting shot with a lot of potential.', '2003-06-27 07:54:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(339977, 26029, 6349, '<td valign="top">I think you would have benefited by taking this shot at a different time of day when the sun wasn''t so direct and harsh.  The light is really overpowering the image and taking away from the subtle shades of greens that I know are there.  In the right light they would dynamically play.  Really nice compostion on this, although it may be a tad bit heavy on the right.</td>', 'I think you would have benefited by taking this shot at a different time of day when the sun wasn''t so direct and harsh.  The light is really overpowering the image and taking away from the subtle shades of greens that I know are there.  In the right light they would dynamically play.  Really nice compostion on this, although it may be a tad bit heavy on the right.', '2003-06-27 07:56:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(339979, 26201, 3735, '<td valign="top">Wow !! Dad used to do this when i was a little girl. this really brings back memories. But i didnt thank people did this anymore . hahah   9</td>', 'Wow !! Dad used to do this when i was a little girl. this really brings back memories. But i didnt thank people did this anymore . hahah   9', '2003-06-27 07:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
