(343948, 26150, 3102, '<td valign="top">Dang, you must be pretty tall!  :)  It''s always interesting to see things from this vantage point -- it''s amazing how much our world tends to look like a big puzzle.</td>', 'Dang, you must be pretty tall!  :)  It''s always interesting to see things from this vantage point -- it''s amazing how much our world tends to look like a big puzzle.', '2003-07-01 22:07:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(343949, 26260, 9462, '<td valign="top">Yikes! That roof looks like it''s gonna go at any minute... Love the sky in this pic.</td>', 'Yikes! That roof looks like it''s gonna go at any minute... Love the sky in this pic.', '2003-07-01 22:08:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(343950, 26102, 3102, '<td valign="top">I''m sure it has been pointed out to you over &amp; over again, but the grain and awkward tilt are definitely a big distraction here, I''m afraid.</td>', 'I''m sure it has been pointed out to you over & over again, but the grain and awkward tilt are definitely a big distraction here, I''m afraid.', '2003-07-01 22:08:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(343956, 26201, 5822, '<td valign="top">What a way to slaughter a gentle and loving animal !!!  Who knows if this pig is even dead yet... and they''re cutting it up already. Makes me want to scream !<br/> <br/>It''s hard to tell yet just where you stand on this but it''s a good photojournalistic picture depicting a part of life that most people would rather not see.  I particularly like the expression that you''ve captured in the man''s face holding the knife on the left.  <br/> <br/>If you have a "heart" then this photo is evocative and emotive. If not, then it merely exhibits the technique of a cold and calculated death with good exposure and focus as there''s no question how this animal died..a slow torturous boil to death followed by a skinning and butchering.  Guess I"m of the former type and judging by your title, you are of the latter type.  <br/> <br/>I''m still giving you a high mark.</td>', 'What a way to slaughter a gentle and loving animal !!!  Who knows if this pig is even dead yet... and they''re cutting it up already. Makes me want to scream ! It''s hard to tell yet just where you stand on this but it''s a good photojournalistic picture depicting a part of life that most people would rather not see.  I particularly like the expression that you''ve captured in the man''s face holding the knife on the left.   If you have a "heart" then this photo is evocative and emotive. If not, then it merely exhibits the technique of a cold and calculated death with good exposure and focus as there''s no question how this animal died..a slow torturous boil to death followed by a skinning and butchering.  Guess I"m of the former type and judging by your title, you are of the latter type.   I''m still giving you a high mark.', '2003-07-01 22:16:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(343962, 26291, 9462, '<td valign="top">LOL</td>', 'LOL', '2003-07-01 22:21:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(343963, 26221, 5822, '<td valign="top">Colors are good but I''m not sure I like the composition. For one, I don''t like the well standing in the middle of the shot and blocking out the main subject.  Secondly, I find the structures not interesting and don''t find that this photo presents anything new or exciting to me, but is just a photo to record the subjects.</td>', 'Colors are good but I''m not sure I like the composition. For one, I don''t like the well standing in the middle of the shot and blocking out the main subject.  Secondly, I find the structures not interesting and don''t find that this photo presents anything new or exciting to me, but is just a photo to record the subjects.', '2003-07-01 22:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(343971, 26250, 5822, '<td valign="top">I think some fill flash would have brightened up the lavender flowers and prevented them from being overshadowed by the more colorful sunset in the background.</td>', 'I think some fill flash would have brightened up the lavender flowers and prevented them from being overshadowed by the more colorful sunset in the background.', '2003-07-01 22:31:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(343974, 26095, 5822, '<td valign="top">Dynamic capture of waterfall and bird and the lighting is excellent.  Just a couple of suggestions...First, I would have liked more of a close up of the bird, as it kind of gets lost in the falls. Not zoom in all the way, but closer than you are.  Secondly, I think it would have been more effective of an image in color. Well done, nonetheless.</td>', 'Dynamic capture of waterfall and bird and the lighting is excellent.  Just a couple of suggestions...First, I would have liked more of a close up of the bird, as it kind of gets lost in the falls. Not zoom in all the way, but closer than you are.  Secondly, I think it would have been more effective of an image in color. Well done, nonetheless.', '2003-07-01 22:36:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(343977, 25938, 3015, '<td valign="top">I like this picture very much. The tree is on a rule of 1/3 and the water is wonderful for a balance. I think to hide the tree in back can help.  7</td>', 'I like this picture very much. The tree is on a rule of 1/3 and the water is wonderful for a balance. I think to hide the tree in back can help.  7', '2003-07-01 22:39:48.000000', NULL, 1),
