(345460, 26250, 509, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all for the comments.  As I predicted many thought it needed more light, but this is the look I was going for.  I wanted the sunset to be a little more powerful than the flower.  Tranquility was what I was going for</td>', 'Thanks to all for the comments.  As I predicted many thought it needed more light, but this is the look I was going for.  I wanted the sunset to be a little more powerful than the flower.  Tranquility was what I was going for', '2003-07-02 18:01:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(345492, 26200, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very nice macro!  Wonderful details.  The back end and wings are perfect, the front end is a little dark/soft, but overall a very, very good image.  (I''m sorry I didn''t vote this challenge)</td>', 'Very nice macro!  Wonderful details.  The back end and wings are perfect, the front end is a little dark/soft, but overall a very, very good image.  (I''m sorry I didn''t vote this challenge)', '2003-07-02 18:23:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(345499, 25431, 1005, '<td valign="top">From the teeth, I''d guess these to be wild boar lower jaws.  The photo quality is excellent.  B&amp;W was a good choice (esp. for the reasons you stated).  It is a bit barbaric, not something I''d hang on MY wall, but the challenge reference is clear to me and the photo quality is plenty high.  (I didn''t vote this challenge, but I''d probably go a 7 or 8)</td>', 'From the teeth, I''d guess these to be wild boar lower jaws.  The photo quality is excellent.  B&W was a good choice (esp. for the reasons you stated).  It is a bit barbaric, not something I''d hang on MY wall, but the challenge reference is clear to me and the photo quality is plenty high.  (I didn''t vote this challenge, but I''d probably go a 7 or 8)', '2003-07-02 18:29:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(345570, 26239, 1005, '<td valign="top">Cool shot!  Great detail!!  I''m not a fan of High Key, but this is done incredibly well, you may have "won me over".  I''d have gone an 7 or maybe an 8 for this one.</td>', 'Cool shot!  Great detail!!  I''m not a fan of High Key, but this is done incredibly well, you may have "won me over".  I''d have gone an 7 or maybe an 8 for this one.', '2003-07-02 19:29:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(345599, 25978, 2333, '<td valign="top">I was astounded to see that you did not place in top three in that challenge. It''s a head shaker. I ran the vote pattern through a statistical analysis to see what was going on, and concluded that there was no unusual voting, just a plain old "gaussian" or normal distribution, albeit with a high standard deviation. I cannot explain this other than to hypothesize that some people just did not understand your submission. <br/>I''ve had a similar experience with one of my submissions, with an even worse score. Granted, my photo was not nearly as good as yours. I voted yours a 10, BTW, one of only a few I have given in over 8,000 votes.<br/>Don''t take to heart the votes of those who seemingly have little imagination. You met the challenge, you submitted a strikingly beautiful, thought-provoking image, and many of us recognized that. Have fun with your photography, and please do continue to contribute to the site.<br/> <br/>Fritz</td>', 'I was astounded to see that you did not place in top three in that challenge. It''s a head shaker. I ran the vote pattern through a statistical analysis to see what was going on, and concluded that there was no unusual voting, just a plain old "gaussian" or normal distribution, albeit with a high standard deviation. I cannot explain this other than to hypothesize that some people just did not understand your submission. I''ve had a similar experience with one of my submissions, with an even worse score. Granted, my photo was not nearly as good as yours. I voted yours a 10, BTW, one of only a few I have given in over 8,000 votes.Don''t take to heart the votes of those who seemingly have little imagination. You met the challenge, you submitted a strikingly beautiful, thought-provoking image, and many of us recognized that. Have fun with your photography, and please do continue to contribute to the site. Fritz', '2003-07-02 20:09:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(345657, 26213, 6134, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the votes guys. My best dpchallenge shot so far :)<br/>I actually held the chicken in my hand with my camera in my other hand, the chicken was very calm and just move its head (the most stupid and funniest bird of all). I took a bunch of photos and picked out the best with my friends help and I think this one was it. I used a polarizer filter and did auto-levels is Photoshop.<br/>Some of you did not like the tractor behind but I wanted that to be, feels more like the country.<br/>Here you can see some of the other shots (the bottom of the page):<br/><a href="//www.myrkur.is/29062003.htm" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.myrkur.is/29062003.htm</a> <br/> <br/>Thanks<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-07-02 20:48:56.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the votes guys. My best dpchallenge shot so far :)I actually held the chicken in my hand with my camera in my other hand, the chicken was very calm and just move its head (the most stupid and funniest bird of all). I took a bunch of photos and picked out the best with my friends help and I think this one was it. I used a polarizer filter and did auto-levels is Photoshop.Some of you did not like the tractor behind but I wanted that to be, feels more like the country.Here you can see some of the other shots (the bottom of the page)://www.myrkur.is/29062003.htm  Thanks', '2003-07-02 21:42:39.000000', '2003-07-02 21:48:56.000000', 0),
(345666, 26326, 3728, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hawkida:</b></div><hr/><i>....The flower(?) in front of the smaller one in very poor focus is horribly distracting and the image is generally quite messy looking. ....The patch of sky we can see is quite washed out.. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes, this is a flower but this isn''t the sky, it''s the bay.  But thank you for your advice.  I''ll keep them in mind ;o)</td>', 'Originally posted by hawkida:....The flower(?) in front of the smaller one in very poor focus is horribly distracting and the image is generally quite messy looking. ....The patch of sky we can see is quite washed out..   Yes, this is a flower but this isn''t the sky, it''s the bay.  But thank you for your advice.  I''ll keep them in mind ;o)', '2003-07-02 21:49:14.000000', NULL, 0),
