(347076, 26012, 9393, '<td valign="top">Indeed, most people would see this an an urban <br/>scene although this was taken in a rural Qinghai province of Northeast China (one of the poorest areas of the country). The tiled pavement and the big blue farming vehecle have indeed been deceptive-not to mention the colourful outfits of the kids. The lack of rural feels, of country atmosphere and environment could be attributable to the administrators of Qinghai for being able to present such an image of a "city" life to our DPC colleagues. The very reason to submit this pic is to simply show the cute side of the kids hanging on to one another in such a manner!. Very much appreciated, however, that you kindly took time to comment.:-)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Indeed, most people would see this an an urban scene although this was taken in a rural Qinghai province of Northeast China (one of the poorest areas of the country). The tiled pavement and the big blue farming vehecle have indeed been deceptive-not to mention the colourful outfits of the kids. The lack of rural feels, of country atmosphere and environment could be attributable to the administrators of Qinghai for being able to present such an image of a "city" life to our DPC colleagues. The very reason to submit this pic is to simply show the cute side of the kids hanging on to one another in such a manner!. Very much appreciated, however, that you kindly took time to comment.:-) ', '2003-07-04 16:10:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(347122, 26079, 714, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone!!!  You are all really great.  <br/> <br/>This is a picture of my son about 10 miles out of town. Great place to take pictures.  I took it in sepia tones in my camera settings. Messed with the contrast just a tad.  No cropping done.  It was an overcast day.  I am not sure why the sky looks so pink with the sepia settings from my camera. I liked it though.<br/> <br/>I appreciate the critiques and comments from everyone. Thank you!<br/>Sonja</td>', 'Thanks everyone!!!  You are all really great.   This is a picture of my son about 10 miles out of town. Great place to take pictures.  I took it in sepia tones in my camera settings. Messed with the contrast just a tad.  No cropping done.  It was an overcast day.  I am not sure why the sky looks so pink with the sepia settings from my camera. I liked it though. I appreciate the critiques and comments from everyone. Thank you!Sonja', '2003-07-04 17:19:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(347194, 26135, 6870, '<td valign="top">I love the multiple layers of tones here. Very nice composition!</td>', 'I love the multiple layers of tones here. Very nice composition!', '2003-07-04 19:10:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(347221, 26237, 3279, '<td valign="top">Well, I guess the lesson to learn here is that my laptop screen isn''t very good for image work - looking at it back on my ''real'' monitor the bright sunlight is a lot more obvious.<br/> <br/>In my defense, I was submitting from a foreign country, on my laptop, via an infared link to my mobile phone on an international call to my ISP, so it''s hardly surprising it wasn''t a masterpiece :-)</td>', 'Well, I guess the lesson to learn here is that my laptop screen isn''t very good for image work - looking at it back on my ''real'' monitor the bright sunlight is a lot more obvious. In my defense, I was submitting from a foreign country, on my laptop, via an infared link to my mobile phone on an international call to my ISP, so it''s hardly surprising it wasn''t a masterpiece :-)', '2003-07-04 20:03:23.000000', NULL, 0),
