(362927, 26270, 1647, '<td valign="top">Pseudo Critique Club<br/> <br/>Composition: In most respects the composition is very good.  I like the tight crop chosen and the shallow depth of field.  The biggest issue with the composition is that it relies on the photo title to relate it to the challenge...  I cannot tell from the photo alone that the cat is in the country or potentially eyeing up a mouse.  The tongue on the cat is great though - it''s thinking of food!<br/> <br/>Technical Quality: I really like the softness of the colours - it has a very natural feel about it.  The focus is also perfect.  Overall, the soft appears just a fraction dark / underexposed although I wouldn''t have added too much light as it would work against the natural feel of this shot.<br/> <br/>Meeting the Challenge:  I think this is where you suffered the most.  I like the idea  you have chosen but it relies too heavily on the title, rather than the image, to fit the challenge.  Of course, you may not have had any nice scenary to work with.<br/> <br/>Overall:  Technically it''s a good shot and I like the idea but a lack of background or other elements means that the cat is not really placed on a "Country Life" context.  Something else that is typically country (a barn, some straw or even a mouse) would have really helped this shot.<br/></td>', 'Pseudo Critique Club Composition: In most respects the composition is very good.  I like the tight crop chosen and the shallow depth of field.  The biggest issue with the composition is that it relies on the photo title to relate it to the challenge...  I cannot tell from the photo alone that the cat is in the country or potentially eyeing up a mouse.  The tongue on the cat is great though - it''s thinking of food! Technical Quality: I really like the softness of the colours - it has a very natural feel about it.  The focus is also perfect.  Overall, the soft appears just a fraction dark / underexposed although I wouldn''t have added too much light as it would work against the natural feel of this shot. Meeting the Challenge:  I think this is where you suffered the most.  I like the idea  you have chosen but it relies too heavily on the title, rather than the image, to fit the challenge.  Of course, you may not have had any nice scenary to work with. Overall:  Technically it''s a good shot and I like the idea but a lack of background or other elements means that the cat is not really placed on a "Country Life" context.  Something else that is typically country (a barn, some straw or even a mouse) would have really helped this shot.', '2003-07-21 22:28:26.000000', NULL, 0),
