(612740, 26238, 669, '<td valign="top">Very nice composition.  Good job getting the horizon straight whilst focusing on the foreground.  There''s a nice gradient of colour from bottom to top, which helps draw the eye.  I think the main issue is the reeds in the foreground are somewhat unexciting.  That said, the shot has a nice depth to it, which helps a lot.  I think you produced the best shot you could of the subject, but I think maybe it wasn''t the best subjec to choose.<br/> <br/>EDIT: At the time I gave this shot a 6.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-03-07 11:30:57.</i></td>', 'Very nice composition.  Good job getting the horizon straight whilst focusing on the foreground.  There''s a nice gradient of colour from bottom to top, which helps draw the eye.  I think the main issue is the reeds in the foreground are somewhat unexciting.  That said, the shot has a nice depth to it, which helps a lot.  I think you produced the best shot you could of the subject, but I think maybe it wasn''t the best subjec to choose. EDIT: At the time I gave this shot a 6.', '2004-03-07 11:30:10.000000', '2004-03-07 11:30:57.000000', 0),
(683161, 26108, 20661, '<td valign="top">I suspect you know, but what you have a picture of is a horse-drawn side cutter.  It was used to cut hay prior to using a side-rake and then bailing.  It could also be used just to cut weeds.  I rode with my grand-father on one many times.</td>', 'I suspect you know, but what you have a picture of is a horse-drawn side cutter.  It was used to cut hay prior to using a side-rake and then bailing.  It could also be used just to cut weeds.  I rode with my grand-father on one many times.', '2004-04-23 23:53:43.000000', NULL, 0),
